# seed: 1
# requires: hero_ready scene_enter minigame_arm minigame_open minigame_slots_spin minigame_slots_result
# GAME 1 (Slobber Slots), the Evergreen casino.
#
# NOTE on the scene number. docs/gap_analysis.md section 12 says "Retail Evergreen scene 4 (the
# casino) uses `GAME 1`". That is WRONG. I grepped the retail quest data: the only real
# `GAME` opcodes in Evergreen are `GAME 1`, and they all live in
# extracted/worlds/Evergreen/QuestScenes1000.txt. The casino is:
#
#     SCENE 1005  aztec          (QuestScenes1000.txt:93)
#         THEME 0
#         ACTOR 1, "Barker", joshRoyalty, 2, 5, 90
#         SEL 1 / MOVE 1, 15, 80
#         GAME 1                 <- QuestScenes1000.txt:99
#         ' Try your luck!
#         ' Our slots pay the most!
#         END
#
# There are ten such casino scenes in that file (lines 99, 213, 301, 393, 484, 578, 676, 780,
# 882, 979) plus a "Generic Casino" template. Reaching one on foot needs the map walk that
# gets a hero into the casino, which this headless script does not drive deterministically, so
# what is proven here is the GAME opcode path itself: the button arms, the click opens the
# dialog, the spin charges and settles.
#
# `GAME n` does not open anything: FUN_00478E04 (0x478E04) -> FUN_00478673 (0x478673) only
# arms a scene button-bar button. Clicking that button is what opens the dialog via
# FUN_00421563 (0x421563) -- RT_DIALOG 0xA7, 176x111, for game 1.
#
# The port draws the armed button at button_rect(7) = {640-51-51*7, 8, 48, 48} = {283,8,48,48},
# so the click is its centre (306,31). The ORIGINAL registers the GAME button in slot 6
# (FUN_00478E04 passes 6, and FUN_00478673's guard is `slot<0||slot>9`), i.e. {334,8,48,48},
# centre (357,31). One-slot difference, flagged to SceneVM-2 and Main.
#
# SPIN is control id 0x447 at client rect (123,7,46,12) inside the 176x111 dialog, handled by
# 0x466BBB: it charges 10 GP, consumes 6 rand() and starts the reels.
expect boot_menu 900
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text Gambler
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 400
expect map_enter 800
keydown DOWN
wait 40
keyup DOWN
expect scene_enter 400
quit
